{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"RHLW-2026-03e0f8fb77137948","published":"2026-11-24T05:13:35Z","modified":"2026-11-25T15:43:28.341484004Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-102946","CVE-2026-119283","CVE-2026-119284","CVE-2026-75509","GHSA-4pp3-559j-c5c2","GHSA-9pg5-8c7x-5hfx","GHSA-jpxq-7h8p-2q76","GHSA-r74j-q665-7rpj"],"summary":"Lightwell Security Advisory: joserfc 1.7.2+rhlw.1","details":"Red Hat Lightwell has released joserfc 1.7.2+rhlw.1 with backported fixes for CVE-2026-75509, CVE-2026-102946, CVE-2026-119283, and CVE-2026-119284.\n\nCVE-2026-75509: joserfc claim-validation bypass via array-typed single-string claims (iss/sub/jti)\n\nCVE-2026-102946: joserfc: JWS signature verification bypass via empty signatures array in jws.deserialize_json\n\nCVE-2026-119283: joserfc: Unbounded JWE General JSON `recipients` Array Leads to CPU Exhaustion (DoS) via Repeated RSA Private-Key Decryption\n\nCVE-2026-119284: joserfc: Compact JWS size guard allocates attacker-controlled segments before rejection\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for joserfc 1.7.2 from PyPI.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"joserfc","ecosystem":"Red Hat Lightwell:PyPI","purl":"pkg:pypi/joserfc"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"1.7.2"},{"fixed":"1.7.2+rhlw.1"}]}],"versions":["1.7.2"],"database_specific":{"lightwell":{"backport_base_version":"1.7.2","remediated_version":"1.7.2+rhlw.1","repository_url":"https://packages.redhat.com/lightwell/python/remediated/"},"source":"https://github.com/project-lightwell/lightwell-osv/blob/main/advisories/RHLW-2026-03e0f8fb77137948.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2026/75xxx/CVE-2026-75509.json"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://github.com/authlib/joserfc/security/advisories/GHSA-r74j-q665-7rpj"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-75509"},{"type":"FIX","url":"https://github.com/authlib/joserfc/commit/76ee6a59bf5773c0af00b99076c5e19903